(ARG-15 — the flag schema form: a name, two alias strings joined by
 `or`, and `it is a <type>` (LANGUAGE.md:4777-4782).
 Also covers: ARG-14 (declarative schema-first flag parsing exists at
 all), ARG-17 (a boolean flag's presence sets it true — printed as 1),
 ARG-18 (a text flag consumes the next token as text), ARG-19 (a number
 flag consumes the next token and parses it as a number). The
 invocation deliberately mixes the short alias of one flag with the long
 alias of another, so both spellings of the same schema are on trial.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox ARG-15.vox -o p && ./p -v -o out.txt --retries 5
 Args: -v -o out.txt --retries 5
 expected output:
   verbose is 1
   output is out.txt
   retries is 5
   retries doubled is 10
)
a flag called verbose is "-v" or "--verbose", it is a boolean.
a flag called output is "-o" or "--output", it is a text.
a flag called retries is "-r" or "--retries", it is a number.
Parse flags.

Print "verbose is {verbose}".
Print "output is {output}".
Print "retries is {retries}".
a number called doubled is retries multiply 2.
Print "retries doubled is {doubled}".
